ts between  \nThe Alton Railroad Company and other  \ncarriers, as set forth in the list attached  \nhereto and made a part hereof, and cer­\ntain of their employees represented by  \nthe Brotherhood o’ f Locomotive Engi­\nneers and the Brotherhood of Railroad  \nTrainmen, labor organizations; and  \nWHEREAS the dispute has not hereto­\nfore been adjusted under the provisions  \nof the Railway Labor Act, as amended;  \nand\n\"V ^H E R E A S the dispute, in the judg­\nment of the National Mediation Board,  \nthreatens substantially to interrupt in­\nterstate commerce to a degree such as to  \ndeprive the country of essential trans­\nportation service:\nNOW, THEREFORE, by virtue of the  \nauthority vested in me by section 10 of  \nthe Railway Labor Act, as amended (45  \nU.S.C. 160), I hereby create a board of  \nthree members, to be appointed by me, to \ninvestigate said dispute. No member of  \nthe said board shall be pecuniarily or  \notherwise interested in any organization  \nof railway employees or any carrier.\nThe board shall report its findings to  \nthe President with respect to the said dis­\npute within thirty days from the date of  \nthis order.\nAs provide^ by section 10 of the Rail­\nway Labor Act, as amended, from this  \ndate and for thirty days after the board  \nhas made its report to the President, n","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-9702-c8a9604a95.txt","sha256":"0bc6429df9317c7885ece5c89c662f2a5d718e7c736db7e9c7cd620b1ba9ec80","source":{"line":1113,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"cebb596c3223f14ded2066b53eaf0a8ebede706582231f4a4f889113122fa7e1"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:9702\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1946-03-12/pdf/FR-1946-03-12.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: c8a9604a9569ecdb5c28e30351315cddd68602e00efdda9d63f9dc89195b251b\nLocation: 11 FR 2493, PDF pages 1-4 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-19